  "[prose] Focussing on b diversity, again for most of the windows (99.6%) overall $\\beta$ diversity among RNAs protected cells (average $\\beta _ { \\mathrm { S O R } } = 0 . 9 0 8 2 \\pm 0 . 0 5 2 8$ across windows) was mainly caused by spatial turnover $\\left( \\beta _ { \\mathrm { S I M } } = 0 . 7 9 3 9 \\pm 0 . 1 0 5 1 \\right)$ , with only a small contribution from nestedness $\\left( \\beta _ { \\mathrm { N E S } } = 0 . 1 1 4 3 \\pm 0 . 0 6 9 8 \\right)$ . Furthermore,",
  "[prose] RNA protected cells did not perform especially well in terms of overall b TD; 61.3% of windows having values of $\\beta _ { \\mathrm { S O R } }$ in protected cells significantly lower than random expectations, and just 0.04% of windows having significantly higher values for protected cells (Fig. 2c). In the case of turnover, only 2.1% of windows had significantly higher $\\beta _ { \\mathrm { S I M } }$ values in protected cells than random expectations (these cells being clustered between Galicia and the Cantabrian Mountains, at north and north-western of Iberian Peninsula), whilst 19.6% had significantly lower values (Fig. 3a). Finally, 4.3% of the windows had significantly higher nestedness in their network of protected cells than expected by chance, whilst 4.0% had significantly lower values (again grouped between Galicia and the Cantabrian Mountains; Fig. 3b).",
  "[prose] With the Natura 2000 network, similar patterns of b FD were obtained: for most of the windows (98.7%) overall $\\beta$ diversity (average $\\beta _ { \\mathrm { S O R } } = 0 . 8 8 5 8 \\pm 0 . 0 6 7 4$ across windows) was mainly driven by spatial turnover (average $\\beta _ { \\mathrm { S I M } } = 0 . 7 1 3 5 \\pm 0 . 1 1 5 6$ versus $\\beta _ { \\mathrm { N E S } } = 0 . 1 7 2 4 \\pm 0 . 0 6 3 8 )$ . 56.9% of windows had values of b SOR significantly lower in the N2000 network, and no windows had significantly higher values for protected cells (Fig. 4f). Only 0.34% of windows had significantly higher $\\beta _ { \\mathrm { S I M } }$ values in protected cells than random, whilst 36.8% had significantly lower values (Fig. 3g). Finally, 24.2% of windows had significantly higher values of $\\beta _ { \\mathrm { N E S } }$ in their network of protected cells, whilst 1.3% had significantly lower values than expected by chance (Fig. 3h).",
